## Colour roles

Each colour is a role, not a swatch. Roles are declared in `design-tokens.json`
under `color.<group>.<name>` with a `light` and a `dark` value.

| Role | Light | Dark | Used for |
|---|---|---|---|
| `surface.canvas` | {{#ffffff}} | {{#0e0e11}} | {{Page background}} |
| `surface.raised` | {{#f6f6f7}} | {{#18181c}} | {{Cards, panels}} |
| `content.primary` | {{#111113}} | {{#f2f2f4}} | {{Body text}} |
| `content.secondary` | {{#4b4b52}} | {{#b4b4bd}} | {{Supporting text}} |
| `content.muted` | {{#6b6b74}} | {{#8e8e99}} | {{Captions, disabled}} |
| `accent.default` | {{#1f4fd8}} | {{#7aa2ff}} | {{Primary action, links}} |
| `border.default` | {{#d9d9de}} | {{#2c2c33}} | {{Dividers, decorative rules}} |
| `border.strong` | {{#8a8a94}} | {{#6b6b76}} | {{Control boundaries}} |
| `border.focus` | {{#1f4fd8}} | {{#7aa2ff}} | {{Focus ring}} |

Accent is used for **one** action type per screen. Status colours
(`danger`, `warning`, `success`, `info`) are reserved for status only.

